From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atharva Tyagi <tyagiatharva11@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 19:56:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix ioLPDMmode: rho must be processed, and the packed range
 must avoid the fill value

Two bugs, both found by testing the mode on real fields before using it.

1. SKIPPING rho SILENTLY DESTROYED EVERY PROGNOSTIC FIELD.
   NORHO is #defined at io_netcdf.c:486 with no matching #undef, so it is in force for the
   writer as well as the reader. Under it, u, v, w, theta and TKE_0 are stored FLUX-
   CONSERVATIVELY and the writer divides each by ioBuffFieldRho -- a buffer filled by a
   memcpy when rho itself comes past in the variable list. Omitting rho therefore did not
   merely drop a field: it divided all five prognostic fields by uninitialised memory.
   Every value came out +/-inf, scale_factor was written as inf and add_offset as nan, and
   nothing anywhere reported an error -- the run exited 0, printed no CORRUPTED, and the
   k0/k1 accuracy check passed because `nan < 1.0` is false.

   Split the one skip test into two: lpdmSkipProcess (rho is processed for its side effect
   on ioBuffFieldRho) and lpdmSkipWrite (rho is still never written).

2. THE FIELD MINIMUM LANDED ON THE DEFAULT FILL VALUE.
   Packing across the full 16-bit range mapped each field's minimum onto -32767, which is
   netCDF's default fill for NC_SHORT. Any reader with auto-masking enabled -- which is the
   default in netCDF4-python -- then treats the slowest and coldest cells as MISSING. The
   maxima were perfect and the minima read back as -32767, which is exactly the kind of
   half-right output that survives a cursory check.

   Pack into [-32000, +32000] instead. The fill value becomes unreachable by data and no
   _FillValue attribute is needed, which is just as well because netCDF will not accept one
   after the variable holds data. 64000 levels instead of 65534 is 2.3% coarser.

Verified against the fp32 dump the test restarted from: endpoints reproduce exactly, and

    field   max|err|    rms        rms / range
    u       6.5e-05     3.7e-05    4.5e-06
    w       2.5e-05     1.4e-05    4.5e-06
    theta   1.5e-04     8.9e-05    4.6e-06

1.4e-05 m/s of rms error on w against sigma_w ~ 0.36 m/s is 0.004% -- an order of magnitude
better than IEEE fp16 over the same fields, because packing spends all 16 bits on the range
that is actually present instead of on an exponent.

Output: 42.7 MB per dump against 170 MB full, so a 30-min window at 5 s is 15.4 GB rather
than 61 GB. Geometry appears in the first file of a run and is omitted thereafter.
---
 SRC/IO/io_netcdf.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/SRC/IO/io_netcdf.c b/SRC/IO/io_netcdf.c
index b0a2fce..176809a 100644
--- a/SRC/IO/io_netcdf.c
+++ b/SRC/IO/io_netcdf.c
@@ -52,14 +52,30 @@ static int lpdmIsKept(const char *n){
         ||(!strcmp(n,"fricVel"))||(!strcmp(n,"z0m"))||(!strcmp(n,"invOblen"))
         ||(!strcmp(n,"time"));
 }
-/* Should this variable be written to THIS file? */
-static int lpdmSkip(const char *n){
+/* Should this variable be WRITTEN to this file? */
+static int lpdmSkipWrite(const char *n){
    if(ioLPDMmode == 0){ return 0; }
    if(!lpdmIsKept(n)){ return 1; }
    if(lpdmIsGeometry(n) && (lpdmFileCount > 0)){ return 1; }   /* geometry: first file only */
    return 0;
 }
 
+/* Should this variable be PROCESSED (gathered and un-flux-converted) at all?
+ *
+ * rho must be, even though it is never written. NORHO is #defined at io_netcdf.c:486 and
+ * has no matching #undef, so it is in force for the writer too: u, v, w, theta and TKE_0
+ * are stored FLUX-CONSERVATIVELY and the writer divides each by ioBuffFieldRho, a buffer
+ * that is populated by a memcpy when rho itself comes past in the variable list. Skipping
+ * rho therefore does not merely omit a field -- it divides all five prognostic fields by
+ * uninitialised memory, and they come out inf with no error anywhere. rho precedes them in
+ * the registry, so processing it and simply not writing it restores the conversion.
+ */
+static int lpdmSkipProcess(const char *n){
+   if(ioLPDMmode == 0){ return 0; }
+   if(!strcmp(n, "rho")){ return 0; }
+   return !lpdmIsKept(n);
+}
+
 int dimids[MAXDIMS];
 size_t count[MAXDIMS];
 size_t start[MAXDIMS];
@@ -741,7 +757,7 @@ int ioDefineNetCDFoutFileVars(int ncid){
    /* For each entry in the ioVarsList, def the var */
    ptr = getFirstVarFromList();
    while(ptr != NULL){
-      if(lpdmSkip(ptr->name)){ ptr = ptr->next; continue; }
+      if(lpdmSkipWrite(ptr->name)){ ptr = ptr->next; continue; }
       /* define the variable */
       if (!strcmp(ptr->type,"float")){ 
          if((ioLPDMmode == 1) && lpdmIsPacked(ptr->name)){
@@ -854,7 +870,7 @@ int ioPutNetCDFoutFileVars(int ncid, int Nx, int Ny, int Nz, int Nh){
    /* For each entry in the ioVarsList, "put" the var */
    ptr = getFirstVarFromList();
    while(ptr != NULL){
-      if(lpdmSkip(ptr->name)){ ptr = ptr->next; continue; }
+      if(lpdmSkipProcess(ptr->name)){ ptr = ptr->next; continue; }
 //#define NORHO  //if defined, it was in ioGetNetCDFinFileVars up above
 #ifdef NORHO
    float * rhofield;
@@ -984,17 +1000,25 @@ int ioPutNetCDFoutFileVars(int ncid, int Nx, int Ny, int Nz, int Nh){
    fflush(stdout);
 #endif
          if (mpi_rank_world==0){
-           if((ioLPDMmode == 1) && lpdmIsPacked(ptr->name)){
+           if(lpdmSkipWrite(ptr->name)){
+             /* processed for its side effect on ioBuffFieldRho, but not written */
+           }else if((ioLPDMmode == 1) && lpdmIsPacked(ptr->name)){
              /* CF packing over this file's actual range: value = scale*stored + offset.
-                65534 (not 65536) of the 16-bit range is used so both endpoints are
-                representable and -32768 stays free as a fill value. */
+                The range is [-32000, +32000], NOT the full 16 bits, and that matters: the
+                DEFAULT netCDF fill value for NC_SHORT is -32767, so mapping a field's
+                minimum onto -32767 makes every reader with auto-masking on treat the
+                coldest/slowest cells as MISSING. Staying inside +/-32000 leaves the fill
+                value unreachable by data and needs no _FillValue attribute (which cannot
+                be added after the variable holds data anyway). The cost is 64000 levels
+                instead of 65534 -- 2.3% coarser, against a quantisation that is already
+                four orders of magnitude below the estimator's own noise. */
              lpdmMin = ioBuffField[0];
              lpdmMax = ioBuffField[0];
              for(lpdmIdx = 1; lpdmIdx < (long long)numElems; lpdmIdx++){
                if(ioBuffField[lpdmIdx] < lpdmMin){ lpdmMin = ioBuffField[lpdmIdx]; }
                if(ioBuffField[lpdmIdx] > lpdmMax){ lpdmMax = ioBuffField[lpdmIdx]; }
              }
-             lpdmScale  = (lpdmMax - lpdmMin)/65534.0f;
+             lpdmScale  = (lpdmMax - lpdmMin)/64000.0f;
              if(lpdmScale <= 0.0f){ lpdmScale = 1.0f; }  /* constant field */
              lpdmOffset = 0.5f*(lpdmMax + lpdmMin);
              lpdmPackBuff = (short *) malloc(((size_t)numElems)*sizeof(short));
